1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:00,901
On Garuda,

2
00:00:00,901 --> 00:00:05,810
Krishna and Satyabhama see the fort holding 16,100 captive princesses.

3
00:00:05,930 --> 00:00:08,180
This is the true story of Choti Diwali.

4
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:10,941
Lord Ram returns tomorrow on Amavasya,

5
00:00:10,941 --> 00:00:14,391
but tonight belongs to Krishna on Narak Chaturdashi.

6
00:00:14,391 --> 00:00:15,320
Pragjyotishpur

7
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:16,668
Meaning Narakasur,

8
00:00:16,668 --> 00:00:19,280
king of Assam and son of Mother Earth,

9
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:19,830
Bhudevi.

10
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:21,363
Yet blinded by his power,

11
00:00:21,363 --> 00:00:24,210
he even stole the earrings of divine mother Aditi.

12
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:27,688
He imprisoned 16,100 princesses in his palace.

13
00:00:27,688 --> 00:00:30,250
At the gods' plea, Krishna arrived.

14
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:33,302
The fort was surrounded by walls of mountains,

15
00:00:33,302 --> 00:00:34,710
fire, water, and wind.

16
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:36,501
And at the gates stood Mura,

17
00:00:36,501 --> 00:00:37,780
a five-headed demon.

18
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:40,819
Krishna broke down every wall and destroyed Mura.

19
00:00:40,819 --> 00:00:43,150
That is why one of his names is Murari.

20
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:45,940
Then Narakasur arrived riding an elephant,

21
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:48,607
and the Sudarshan Chakra shattered his pride.

22
00:00:48,607 --> 00:00:50,030
The palace doors opened.

23
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:52,605
The princesses locked in darkness for years...

24
00:00:52,605 --> 00:00:54,910
Came out into the light for the first time.

25
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:57,979
It is said in the joy of that liberation...

26
00:00:57,979 --> 00:00:59,155
Lamps are lit today.

27
00:00:59,155 --> 00:01:01,860
That is why today people bathe applying oil...

28
00:01:03,370 --> 00:01:04,673
And in many homes,

29
00:01:04,673 --> 00:01:07,640
an evening lamp for Yama. Narak is not...

30
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:09,953
Anger, laziness, bad habits,

31
00:01:09,953 --> 00:01:11,597
this is our Narkasur.

32
00:01:11,597 --> 00:01:14,260
Tonight is the night to let it go.

33
00:01:14,370 --> 00:01:16,085
Harivansh Rai Bachchan wrote...

34
00:01:16,085 --> 00:01:17,082
the night is dark,

35
00:01:17,082 --> 00:01:19,350
but when is it forbidden to light a lamp?

36
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:21,730
Which darkness will you leave behind today?

37
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:24,005
Write a single word in the comments.

38
00:01:24,005 --> 00:01:26,290
Jai Shri Krishna, happy Chhoti Diwali.

